{"name":"Tempered Chocolate","hex":"#772211","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tempered","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a specified disposition or temper.","Pertaining to the metallurgical process for finishing metals."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of temper"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tempered"},{"term":"chocolate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from ground roasted cocoa beans.","A drink made by dissolving this food in boiling milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or containing chocolate.","Having a dark reddish-brown colour/color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tempered chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Tempering is a technique applied in chocolate production to create chocolate that is glossy, has a good snap and smoother texture and is more resistant to chocolate bloom. It involves cooling liquid chocolate while agitating it until a small amount of cocoa butter crystallizes. The liquid is then heated to maintain only the most stable crystal forms, which serve as nuclei for the rest of the cocoa butter to solidify around."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Couverture_chocolate_samples%2C_tempered_and_untempered.jpg/330px-Couverture_chocolate_samples%2C_tempered_and_untempered.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tempered_chocolate"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate"},{"title":"Chocolate (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color chocolate or cocoa brown is a shade of brown that resembles chocolate. At right is displayed the color traditionally called chocolate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Chocolate02.jpg/330px-Chocolate02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Chocolate_Tempering_Machine.jpg/500px-Chocolate_Tempering_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Chocolate_Tempering_Machine.jpg/500px-Chocolate_Tempering_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chocolate tempering machine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocolate_Tempering_Machine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png/330px-Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png/330px-Kakaw_%28Mayan_word%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Maya glyph for cacao","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKakaw_(Mayan_word).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Aztec._Man_Carrying_a_Cacao_Pod%2C_1440-1521.jpg/500px-Aztec._Man_Carrying_a_Cacao_Pod%2C_1440-1521.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Aztec._Man_Carrying_a_Cacao_Pod%2C_1440-1521.jpg/500px-Aztec._Man_Carrying_a_Cacao_Pod%2C_1440-1521.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mexica. Man Carrying a Cacao Pod,